61,3,1,talk,Midori,,"Looking at the options, Candidate A offers a hosted suite with a regional service team, which provides the single point of accountability and integrated structure we discussed. It seems much safer than the modular approach of Candidate C.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,"@Midori, I disagree. Candidate A's ""fixed configuration"" sounds like a disaster for our fragmented hardware and peak-season chaos. Candidate D is the only one with an engineering team present through rollout and a focus on transport operators.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,May,,"@Ryuji, I'm wary of Candidate D. ""Deployed on our own servers"" sounds like a repeat of the dispatch tool nightmare where we skip upgrades because we can't handle the testing. We need a hosted solution to avoid rotting in place.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Misaki,,"@May, I agree. Candidate D puts the maintenance burden back on our shrinking admin team. Candidate B's partner-led training and configurable workflows might be better for our supervisors, but Candidate A's hosted suite is the most stable.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"@Midori, you are correct about Candidate C; it is a financial minefield. Between A and B, A's hosted suite suggests the bundled pricing I desire, whereas B's marketplace could lead to those creeping, separate costs.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Midori,,"@Ryuji, I understand your concern about the ""fixed"" nature of A, but D's on-premise model risks the very lack of ownership I fear. A single regional service team is far more accountable than our own exhausted staff.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Midori, accountability is useless if the system doesn't work in the yard. A ""fixed configuration"" will ignore our old scanners and peak-season reality. D's engineering team is the only way to ensure it actually survives the rollout.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,May,,"@Ryuji, having an engineering team for a few weeks doesn't solve the long-term rot. Once they leave, we're back to skipping upgrades on our own servers. A hosted suite is the only way to ensure the system stays current.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Ryuji, I'm worried that D's on-site team is a temporary fix. Once they leave, the burden falls on our two remaining admins. A hosted system like A or B removes that technical weight from our staff.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Ryuji, while I admire your commitment to the yard, we cannot ignore the budget. Candidate D's on-premise model often hides massive long-term maintenance costs. Candidate A offers the most predictable financial and operational package.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Midori,,"@Ryuji, I hear you, but we can't let one concern outweigh the systemic risks. Candidate A provides the balance of accountability and stability we need. I believe it is the most sustainable choice for the company.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Midori, I cannot ignore the risk of a total operational collapse during peak season. A system that doesn't fit our hardware is a failure. However, if the majority prefers A, I will concede, though I remain skeptical.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,May,,"@Ryuji, I appreciate your caution, but we can't keep solving today's problems by creating tomorrow's technical debt. Candidate A is the only one that guarantees we won't be stuck with a digital fossil in five years.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Misaki,,"@Ryuji, I understand your fear, but we simply don't have the people to manage Candidate D. Candidate A's hosted model is the only way to protect our staff from burnout while ensuring the system actually functions.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,"It seems we have reached a consensus of necessity. Candidate A avoids the financial fragmentation of C, the technical decay of D, and the potential cost-creep of B. It is the most rational choice for our budget and our sanity.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Midori,,"I am glad we could find common ground. Candidate A addresses our need for accountability, financial predictability, and operational stability. I will cast my vote for Meridian Systems.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Ryuji,,"I still have reservations about the fixed configuration, but I cannot fight the entire panel. For the sake of a unified decision and the support of the administrative staff, I will vote for Meridian Systems.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,May,,I'm completely on board. It's the only option that keeps us from rotting in place while providing a cohesive structure. I vote for Meridian Systems.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Misaki,,"I agree. Given our staffing shortages and the need for a sustainable transition, Candidate A is the most responsible choice. I vote for Meridian Systems.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
80,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,"The logic is sound and the financial risk is minimized. To avoid the ghosts of future invoices and the chaos of fragmented support, I also vote for Meridian Systems.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
